// `hash` is a reserved method name: the language gives it a meaning, and a
// type may not give it another. Nothing in the program calls it -- the
// runtime does, through a pointer in the type's TypeInfo -- so there is no
// use site to put the message on, and the shape is checked where it is
// written.
type Key {
    int v;
}

str Key.hash() {
    return str(v);
}
